Official AISIX 1.9.0 ARM64 container, pinned by immutable image digest. Configuration and provider resources are mounted read-only. The gateway and mock use the same host network, with the gateway constrained to the standard four-core slice.

One static resource configuration wires the mock-backed OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses and Anthropic models. Fresh correctness probes establish the served pairs for this build; historical declarations from AISIX 0.10 are not reused as current evidence.

vertex upstream # Pinned v1.9.0 supports api_base override and dummy access-token/project/region credentials for local Gemini adapter checks
bedrock upstream # Pinned adapter accepts api_base plus explicit dummy AWS credentials; Nova uses Converse
apis upstream # Empty API declaration on Chat-only provider prevents Responses ingress silently selecting the Responses upstream; separate alias retains Responses routing

Thirteen pairs passed exact recorder and response-content checks in aisix-protocol-preflight.json. Cohere chat is not one of the five native adapter families; specialized Cohere embedding/reranking support is outside this chat matrix.

The pinned ProviderApis schema documents an explicit empty apis map as a Chat-only upstream contract; dispatch.rs::serves_natively_with then bridges Responses ingress into Chat. The separate Responses provider retains its native default. These are static upstream contracts, not per-cell reconfiguration or performance settings. Source: https://github.com/api7/aisix/blob/7e070f0bde3f653c3b197ed18c5b9205b866a4c5/crates/aisix-core/src/models/provider_key.rs
